# Products an earlier build installed at a path no rule makes any more.
#
# An install puts a product where its rule says, and nothing ever takes one
# away from where an older rule put it.  A disk mkimage builds starts empty,
# so it never has one; a disk rebuilt in place -- ipnxbuild on the machine
# itself, which is how the 8 Oct 2026 golden was made -- keeps every product
# that has moved, beside its new copy, for good.  Found by reading that golden
# from the host: three files older than its last build that nothing in it
# wrote, each a fix that changed where its rule installs, and each already on
# the 18 Sep golden too.
#
# ipnxbuild removes each path listed here from the disk it is building, after
# a build whose every step succeeded -- a failed step can mean the new copy
# was never installed, and the old one is then the only one there is.  One
# path per row, relative to the root of that disk; anything after it on the
# row is a note.  A row stays after its file is gone: the next disk restored
# from an older archive has it again.
